1
00:00:00,350 --> 00:00:05,752
Meet Ambi. A voice-first companion that turns a request into visible action.

2
00:00:07,750 --> 00:00:10,950
I’m going to check nine times six in Calculator now.

3
00:00:11,100 --> 00:00:13,550
The result is fifty-four.

4
00:00:13,950 --> 00:00:20,084
On the Mac, Ambi opens Calculator and completes a calculation. This separate recorded
test shows

5
00:00:20,084 --> 00:00:23,535
nine times nine, with eighty-one displayed in the app.

6
00:00:27,950 --> 00:00:34,469
On Windows, Ambi works in Notepad. This recorded test includes an editing mistake,
recovery, and

7
00:00:34,469 --> 00:00:37,864
a saved note whose text was independently checked.

8
00:00:52,200 --> 00:00:56,300
I saved and checked the test note, and its text matches exactly.

9
00:00:56,800 --> 00:01:02,500
There was a brief mistaken edit to another document, but it was undone right away and
not saved.

10
00:01:04,550 --> 00:01:09,088
A coloured frame and a separate Stop task button show when Ambi is acting.

11
00:01:09,088 --> 00:01:12,645
Stop was tested on a separate task, and the frame cleared.

12
00:01:16,050 --> 00:01:20,441
Connections offer browser handoffs to ChatGPT, Claude and Gemini.

13
00:01:20,441 --> 00:01:24,156
Authenticated chat automation is not demonstrated here.

14
00:01:25,550 --> 00:01:31,483
Built and tested on Mac and Windows. Linux is a source preview. Ambi is a working
prototype, with

15
00:01:31,483 --> 00:01:33,440
clear controls and room to grow.
